WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:05.280
Jay and Michael were a pair of urban exploration&nbsp;
YouTubers looking for their big break.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:09.360
You might remember their video exploring&nbsp;
the dead mall on the outskirts of your town,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:14.240
or the supposedly “haunted” 1950s&nbsp;
insane asylum out in the styx,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:21.040
but you certainly won’t find these videos&nbsp;
anywhere online. After The Incident at SCP - 823,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.040 --> 00:00:26.800
all of their content was scrubbed away from even&nbsp;
the most comprehensive internet archives. “Why?”&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:32.720
you ask. Because these unfortunate urban explorers&nbsp;
decided that their big break would be exploring&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:38.640
a certain abandoned theme park. And it would&nbsp;
be one of the last decisions they ever made.

00:00:38.640 --> 00:00:43.680
Michael and Jay had heard rumors about the&nbsp;
theme park. Its name was lost to time, as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.680 --> 00:00:49.520
was the date of its opening and closing, and the&nbsp;
reason it was even abandoned in the first place.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.520 --> 00:00:54.880
Even some of the most hardcore urban explorers&nbsp;
didn’t dare to tread there. Something about it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.880 --> 00:01:00.960
a good friend had once told Jay, just didn’t feel&nbsp;
right. Sometimes, if you dare to venture into the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:07.520
forest near the theme park at night, you can&nbsp;
still hear music. The jolly, piping tunes of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.520 --> 00:01:14.720
rides and carnival stands still beckoning. As&nbsp;
if to say, “We’re still here. Come and play.”

00:01:14.720 --> 00:01:18.240
Of course, none of this frightened Jay&nbsp;
and Michael. They could already smell&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.240 --> 00:01:21.680
the sponsorships from headlamp&nbsp;
and compact camera companies.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.680 --> 00:01:26.480
No amount of anxiety would stop them from&nbsp;
making their doomed trip to the so-called&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.480 --> 00:01:31.840
“Carnival of Horrors.” It’s a terrible shame -&nbsp;
if they’d listened to the stories of this place&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.840 --> 00:01:37.600
about how unnatural and evil it could&nbsp;
be...They might still be alive today.

00:01:37.600 --> 00:01:43.040
Like all the best urban explorers, they arrived&nbsp;
at the woods near the abandoned theme park in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.040 --> 00:01:48.560
the dead of night. They ignored the signs warning&nbsp;
them about everything from structural instability,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.560 --> 00:01:54.880
to dangerous wild animals, to asbestos.&nbsp;
Nothing would keep them out. Nothing.

00:01:54.880 --> 00:01:58.960
They reached the abandoned theme park not&nbsp;
long after, though it was a mere shell of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.960 --> 00:02:04.160
its former self. During the several decades&nbsp;
of abandonment, nature had reclaimed it.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.160 --> 00:02:09.600
The ferris wheel was covered in overgrown ivy&nbsp;
and the carnival stands were blanketed with mold.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.160 --> 00:02:14.880
As the duo swept through the grounds with their&nbsp;
flashlights and cameras, they saw a faded sign&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.880 --> 00:02:17.760
that bore the words “Thriller Chiller” - next&nbsp;
to the rusty skeleton of what had once been the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.760 --> 00:02:22.000
park’s most popular roller coaster.&nbsp;
They also took their time to marvel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:27.040
at the exceptionally creepy-looking Tunnel&nbsp;
of Love, the broken down House of Mirrors,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.040 --> 00:02:31.920
and a huge, grinning statue of the&nbsp;
park’s former mascot, Happy Hippo.

00:02:31.920 --> 00:02:35.040
This theme park was like something&nbsp;
out of a nightmare, which, naturally,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.040 --> 00:02:40.400
made it potential video gold. But as the&nbsp;
excited duo wandered further into the park,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.400 --> 00:02:45.520
they couldn’t help but notice the quiet,&nbsp;
tinny carnival music. Music that seemed to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.520 --> 00:02:50.960
be drawing them closer. Michael asked Jay if&nbsp;
he could hear the strange, impossible music,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.960 --> 00:02:55.840
and felt a chill creep in when he answered&nbsp;
that he did. Could all of the stories be true?

00:02:55.840 --> 00:03:01.280
They were lost in thought, but their legs kept&nbsp;
moving. They were getting closer to something now.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.280 --> 00:03:04.880
They could feel a presence. And&nbsp;
was that music getting louder?

00:03:04.880 --> 00:03:09.920
An instant later, though, another sound&nbsp;
cut through the silence - BANG! BANG!

00:03:09.920 --> 00:03:15.120
It echoed out through the still night air.&nbsp;
Birds flew from their perches in the trees.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.120 --> 00:03:19.520
Jay and Michael both fell to the ground,&nbsp;
dead, their heads taken off by the fifty&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.520 --> 00:03:24.480
caliber rounds of a highly-trained Mobile&nbsp;
Task Force Sniper on the payroll of the SCP&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.480 --> 00:03:29.440
Foundation. Their recording equipment, along&nbsp;
with their bodies, were taken and destroyed.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.440 --> 00:03:34.320
Any trace of them was scrubbed from the internet.&nbsp;
It may seem a little harsh, but a bullet to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.320 --> 00:03:39.120
the head is a much kinder fate than what would&nbsp;
have awaited these two if they’d kept walking.

00:03:39.120 --> 00:03:44.240
That’s because the Carnival of Horrors is&nbsp;
no dark fairytale. The rumors are all true,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:44.240 --> 00:03:48.640
and something really is waiting in the&nbsp;
dark. That’s why this abandoned theme park&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.640 --> 00:03:56.320
is known to the SCP Foundation as SCP - 823,&nbsp;
a Euclid class anomaly with a violent history.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:56.320 --> 00:04:01.360
What’s even more unnerving is that the researchers&nbsp;
studying 823 have repeatedly implored the O5&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:01.360 --> 00:04:07.360
Council to increase the park’s classification to&nbsp;
Keter and allocate more resources for containment,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.360 --> 00:04:11.920
only to be denied. But after you’ve heard&nbsp;
about the horrors that unfolded there,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:11.920 --> 00:04:16.160
and the danger it poses, you’ll&nbsp;
probably take the researchers’ side.

00:04:16.160 --> 00:04:21.760
The park is divided into two different zones:&nbsp;
The Yellow Zone and the Red Zone. There are to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:21.760 --> 00:04:26.720
be at least six members of Foundation personnel&nbsp;
present in the Yellow Zone at all times to ensure&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:26.720 --> 00:04:31.760
that no civilians wander in. Our two urban&nbsp;
explorers earned themselves a death sentence&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.760 --> 00:04:37.440
not just by wandering into the Yellow Zone,&nbsp;
but passing dangerously close to the Red Zone.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.440 --> 00:04:42.800
This is the true epicenter of the park’s&nbsp;
dangerous, anomalous activity. It’s a place so&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:42.800 --> 00:04:48.080
hazardous that anyone entering, whether they’re&nbsp;
a civilian or a member of Foundation staff,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:48.080 --> 00:04:52.720
is to be executed at a distance&nbsp;
by sniper fire without hesitation.

00:04:52.720 --> 00:04:58.080
Once upon a time, though nobody knows exactly&nbsp;
when, there was a theme park that seemed no&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.080 --> 00:05:03.120
different to any other. Eager children and&nbsp;
thrill-seeking teens arrived by the busload,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:03.120 --> 00:05:08.240
ready to stuff their faces with cotton candy&nbsp;
and corn dogs, and then reverse the process on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:08.240 --> 00:05:14.320
a vast array of rollercoasters. But even then&nbsp;
during these good times, there was something&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:14.320 --> 00:05:21.440
dark lurking behind the cheerful facade. Little&nbsp;
by little everyone, visitors and employees alike,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:21.440 --> 00:05:25.920
started falling victim to strange and&nbsp;
horrific accidents around the park.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:25.920 --> 00:05:31.920
Of course, when it comes to theme parks, accidents&nbsp;
come with the territory, but none like this. Here&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:31.920 --> 00:05:37.200
are just a handful of the horrific and mysterious&nbsp;
deaths that occurred while the park was open.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:37.200 --> 00:05:42.880
So strap in, because just like a roller&nbsp;
coaster, this isn’t for the faint of heart.

00:05:42.880 --> 00:05:47.600
A pair of young lovebirds decided they wanted&nbsp;
to enjoy the romance of the Tunnel of Love.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:47.600 --> 00:05:52.720
The two sat in a swan-shaped boat as they&nbsp;
were ferried through darkened passageways.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:52.720 --> 00:05:57.120
Anyone would assume that they were&nbsp;
having a great time, but at some point,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:57.120 --> 00:06:02.000
terrible shrieks of pain and fear began&nbsp;
to echo through the ride. Attendants,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:02.000 --> 00:06:06.880
confused and terrified, stopped the ride and&nbsp;
found that the screaming persisted. Just some&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:06.880 --> 00:06:12.240
stupid teens playing a prank, they figured, and&nbsp;
started the ride again. But when the swan-shaped&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:12.240 --> 00:06:18.400
boat finally exited the Tunnel of Love, the park&nbsp;
employees were greeted to a horrifying sight:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:18.400 --> 00:06:23.840
The two teens, dead, their bodies somehow&nbsp;
fused together at multiple points.

00:06:23.840 --> 00:06:28.240
Another unlucky customer met a gruesome&nbsp;
fate inside the House of Mirrors.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:28.240 --> 00:06:33.040
They entered, but while inside, they were&nbsp;
stalked by a mysterious, carnivorous,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:33.040 --> 00:06:39.920
humanoid entity known as Subject 79. The customer&nbsp;
was pursued and eventually caught by Subject 79,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:39.920 --> 00:06:45.680
and brutally dismembered. Some parts of the body&nbsp;
were fused to the House of Mirrors’ interior while&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:45.680 --> 00:06:51.680
others - like the right arm - were never found.&nbsp;
This customer actually survived their ordeal - and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:51.680 --> 00:06:56.480
whether that’s a happy ending is up to you.
But it wasn’t just the customers at the park&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:56.480 --> 00:07:02.320
who were in danger. A 23-year-old park employee&nbsp;
working a summer job collapsed while entertaining&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:02.320 --> 00:07:07.520
children dressed as the park’s cheerful mascot,&nbsp;
Happy Hippo. It wasn’t uncommon for people to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:07.520 --> 00:07:12.960
get overheated and collapse in the heavy suits&nbsp;
on hot days, but one thing was different here:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:12.960 --> 00:07:17.760
He was screaming, crying, and trying&nbsp;
desperately to remove his mask.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:17.760 --> 00:07:23.840
People rushed to help, but nobody could get the&nbsp;
suit off, and he was declared dead soon after.

00:07:23.840 --> 00:07:25.920
When he was eventually cut out of the suit,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:25.920 --> 00:07:31.040
coroners found that the employee had choked to&nbsp;
death. His mouth, trachea, and lungs were filled&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:31.040 --> 00:07:36.080
with a fibrous substance later determined to&nbsp;
be identical to the stuffing of his costume.

00:07:36.080 --> 00:07:41.120
An intense roller coaster known as the Thriller&nbsp;
Chiller was a magnet for horrific accidents,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:41.120 --> 00:07:43.840
which became more violent and intense over time.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:44.400 --> 00:07:48.560
The first accident seemed like a typical&nbsp;
theme park tragedy - A safety harness&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:48.560 --> 00:07:54.160
failed dropping a rider fifteen feet during an&nbsp;
inverted loop. They landed on the track below,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:54.160 --> 00:07:59.520
breaking their neck and skull, causing instant&nbsp;
death. While this was a tragedy, it wasn’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:59.520 --> 00:08:05.440
exactly anomalous. But the next major accident&nbsp;
on the ride was an entirely different story.

00:08:05.440 --> 00:08:10.960
This time, fifteen people met with disaster&nbsp;
while riding the Thriller Chiller roller coaster.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:10.960 --> 00:08:16.320
Starting from the front and moving back one car&nbsp;
at a time, each group of riders was decapitated by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:16.320 --> 00:08:21.760
blunt force trauma. A new pair of decapitations&nbsp;
appeared to happen at every turn and loop on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:21.760 --> 00:08:27.120
the ride. Forensic scientists still have no&nbsp;
idea how this could have possibly occurred.

00:08:27.120 --> 00:08:33.120
Despite all of these disasters, the park was only&nbsp;
finally abandoned after a day known as “Bloody&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:33.120 --> 00:08:40.320
Sunday”, when the anomalous powers of the location&nbsp;
reached a twenty year peak. It’s believed that 231&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:40.320 --> 00:08:46.400
people were killed during the carnage of that day,&nbsp;
and another seven were horribly maimed. The SCP&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:46.400 --> 00:08:51.520
Foundation contained the Carnival of Horrors not&nbsp;
long after, but the mysterious deaths didn’t even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:51.520 --> 00:08:57.840
end there. Foundation Mobile Task Force Rho-71,&nbsp;
also known as the Origami Toads, were sent in to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:57.840 --> 00:09:03.040
assess containment procedures and discover the&nbsp;
source of all the anomalous deaths. They were&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:03.040 --> 00:09:09.920
unsuccessful though, and instead they merely added&nbsp;
to the list, in exceptionally horrifying ways.

00:09:09.920 --> 00:09:15.040
One agent was found dead, surrounded by empty&nbsp;
grenades and bullet casings. It appeared he’d&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:15.040 --> 00:09:18.960
removed the explosive propellant from&nbsp;
all of his ballistics and consumed it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:18.960 --> 00:09:23.840
dying in the process. Another was found with&nbsp;
his jaw broken, having apparently pulled out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:23.840 --> 00:09:29.120
and inhaled his own teeth, and dying of the&nbsp;
resulting internal damage. The commander&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:29.120 --> 00:09:34.960
got the worst fate of all - so horrifying, in&nbsp;
fact, that we can’t tell you the full details.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:34.960 --> 00:09:40.480
All you need to know is that something was shoved&nbsp;
into his brain that really didn’t belong there.

00:09:40.480 --> 00:09:44.560
The Foundation considered having the entire&nbsp;
park destroyed with a massive airstrike,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:44.560 --> 00:09:51.280
courtesy of the Mobile Task Force Nu-7, aka Hammer&nbsp;
Down. However, the O5 Council denied this request,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:51.280 --> 00:09:54.480
on the basis that the park was&nbsp;
too close to populated land,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:54.480 --> 00:09:58.480
they’d have no plausible cover story for the&nbsp;
bombing, and they don’t even really know if&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:58.480 --> 00:10:02.880
blowing up the park would prevent anomalous&nbsp;
activity from occurring. The Carnival of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:02.880 --> 00:10:09.280
Horrors is here to stay, folks, the Foundation&nbsp;
just hopes to keep it from getting new visitors.&nbsp;

00:10:09.280 --> 00:10:13.360
So then back to why the researchers&nbsp;
want this place upgraded to Keter.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:13.360 --> 00:10:18.560
After all, these classifications aren’t about&nbsp;
how dangerous an anomaly is - they’re about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:18.560 --> 00:10:24.720
how difficult and complicated they are to contain.&nbsp;
But here’s the problem - according to researchers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:24.720 --> 00:10:30.160
the Red Zone - where the dangerous, anomalous&nbsp;
activity is at its peak - isn’t bound to one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:30.160 --> 00:10:35.200
fixed position. It’s changed position at&nbsp;
least three times already, and even worse,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:35.200 --> 00:10:42.000
it appears to be growing. Not seeming so Euclid&nbsp;
class now, is it? After all, you might not even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:42.000 --> 00:10:47.440
need to visit the Carnival of Horrors to be in&nbsp;
grave danger. If it keeps growing then someday&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:47.440 --> 00:10:55.440
soon, the Carnival of Horrors may be visiting you…
Now go check out “SCP - 2000 - Deus Ex Machina”&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:55.440 --> 00:11:04.960
and “SCP - 4205 - In The Eyes of The Beholder”&nbsp;
for more existentially terrifying SCPs!

